{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>If with a tunnel.</b> When he was tunneling into the house." "<b>He has no blood.</b> This is not murder — it is as though he were dead from the outset. Here the Torah taught you: if someone comes to kill you, rise early to kill him. And this one came to kill you — for he knows that no person stands by and stays silent seeing his property taken before his eyes; therefore he came on that condition, that if the owner stands against him he will kill him (Sanhedrin 72a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:45.584665619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}